{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674514",
      "title": "Handling Error Responses via CatchBoundary",
      "lectureOrder": 28,
      "videoOrder": 24,
      "sourceHash": "54a3d36f3d478affa71eb15b6ce5043db5d9d35abfc842446375bef0ed590495",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.36,
          "en": "Now error boundary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.36,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "is super important and helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "for, well, handling errors, but it actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 11.1,
          "en": "only deals with normal errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.1,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "but there is another kind of error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 17.46,
          "en": "that could occur in case of a full stack application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.46,
          "end": 19.98,
          "en": "You could have an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.98,
          "end": 22.143,
          "en": "that's being generated by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.07,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "And to show you what the difference is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 28.59,
          "en": "let me actually generate an error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.59,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "For that, back here in notes jsx, we could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "that we maybe wanna generate some error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 37.11,
          "en": "if we don't find any notes yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.11,
          "end": 39.42,
          "en": "We could check if maybe not notes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.42,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "or if notes dot length is equal to zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "which means we have no notes yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "And in that case, I don't wanna return this MT array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "but instead I wanna generate an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "maybe a 404 response because no notes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "were found. And generating such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 59.1,
          "en": "an error response in Remix is super simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.1,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "You don't use return, but instead the throw keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "and then you don't throw any random data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 68.13,
          "en": "but instead a response, which you can create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.13,
          "end": 71.13,
          "en": "by instantiating the built-in response object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 75.3,
          "en": "which is supported by Norwich JS and the browser or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.3,
          "end": 79.65299999999999,
          "en": "by using a shortcut and using the json function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 83.19,
          "en": "which is imported like the redirect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 84.723,
          "en": "from Remix run node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.74,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "And this json function simply generates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 91.413,
          "en": "a response object which contains some json data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 95.06700000000001,
          "en": "Now the first argument to this json function is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.06700000000001,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "the data that should be included in the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 100.65,
          "en": "And here, that could be an object with a message of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.65,
          "end": 103.533,
          "en": "could not find any notes, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 106.65,
          "en": "The second argument you pass to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "this json function allows you to configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 111.36,
          "en": "this response in greater detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 113.67,
          "en": "For example, you can add a status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.67,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "and here we could set it to 404",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 118.56,
          "en": "to make it clear which kind of response it is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.56,
          "end": 120.693,
          "en": "which kind of error we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 125.79,
          "en": "You can also add a status text, which could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 128.103,
          "en": "not found or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "Now whenever you throw a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 134.55,
          "en": "Remix recognizes this and renders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.55,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "a different component than the error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "Whenever you throw anything but a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 143.1,
          "en": "like some text or a regular object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.1,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "the error boundary will be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "Whenever you return, the default page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "will be used. And whenever you throw a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.78,
          "en": "like a response generated with this json helper function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "and never a component will be rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 162.03,
          "en": "a component which you also should export here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.03,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "in your Route to which it belongs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 167.94,
          "en": "and a component that's called catch boundary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.94,
          "end": 171.78300000000002,
          "en": "because this catches any error responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 174.78,
          "en": "And just like error boundary, you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 174.78,
          "end": 177.78,
          "en": "add it on a per Route level, or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.78,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "add it on the root level, or do both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.81,
          "en": "The root level catch boundary will catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "all unhandled error responses that were",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 189.75,
          "en": "generated anywhere else in the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.75,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "and the Route specific catch boundary will handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 195.603,
          "en": "any error responses related to this Route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.86,
          "end": 199.113,
          "en": "And here, we could then return,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "again, a main block, where we simply output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "a paragraph where we then might want to output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 210.333,
          "en": "the message that's attached to this error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.74,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "To get hold of that data, we can use another special hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 218.253,
          "en": "provided by Remix, the use catch hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.21,
          "end": 220.92000000000002,
          "en": "which of course must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.92000000000002,
          "end": 223.653,
          "en": "from Remix run React in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.32999999999998,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "Now this use catch hook here gives us an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "the caught response, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 235.56,
          "en": "so this error response that was generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 235.56,
          "end": 239.82,
          "en": "or to be precise an object based on that error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.82,
          "end": 242.49,
          "en": "And on that object, we can get hold of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 242.49,
          "end": 244.68,
          "en": "the status code, the status text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.68,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "and the data that's part of the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.98,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "So basically, the kind of things we passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 251.94,
          "en": "to this json function, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.94,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "There I passed some content, a status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "and a status text and that's exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 258,
          "en": "what we can extract with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 260.193,
          "en": "of that data returned by use catch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 261.9,
          "end": 264.72,
          "en": "So here we could then access the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "and get hold of the message property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "if data exists, and if the message property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 273.75,
          "en": "or data is undefined, we could simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 273.75,
          "end": 278.283,
          "en": "use some generic fallback message like data not found,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.45,
          "end": 282.42,
          "en": "and then store that in a message constant and output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "this here in our returned value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 287.55,
          "en": "And this component will now be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 287.55,
          "end": 290.43,
          "en": "by Remix whenever we have an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 290.43,
          "end": 295.323,
          "en": "being thrown by an action or a loader related to this Route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 300.21,
          "en": "If we now save this, and I fix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 300.21,
          "end": 302.46,
          "en": "the notes dot json file name again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.46,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "and I now delete all the notes from this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 311.36,
          "en": "so that we have no notes and we then save everything again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.32,
          "end": 315.87,
          "en": "If we reload, we see this could not find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 315.87,
          "end": 318.54,
          "en": "any notes error message, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 318.54,
          "end": 320.55,
          "en": "is that message we attached to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 320.55,
          "end": 323.673,
          "en": "this error response we're throwing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 326.057,
          "end": 327.9,
          "en": "Now, styling is not great, but we can easily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 327.9,
          "end": 330.6,
          "en": "fix this by adding a special class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.6,
          "end": 334.14,
          "en": "to this paragraph, the info dash message class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334.14,
          "end": 336.783,
          "en": "which is also defined in one of the CSS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.86,
          "end": 340.59000000000003,
          "en": "And with that, it looks a lot better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.59000000000003,
          "end": 342.48,
          "en": "Of course, here we now have the problem that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 342.48,
          "end": 344.73,
          "en": "we can't add any notes anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 344.73,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "because, well, our form is gone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 350.13,
          "en": "and therefore here in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 350.13,
          "end": 351.9,
          "en": "in this catch boundary component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 351.9,
          "end": 356.15999999999997,
          "en": "we also might want to output the new note form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 356.15999999999997,
          "end": 359.01,
          "en": "so that we still can add new notes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 359.01,
          "end": 361.95,
          "en": "like a new note here, and this then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 361.95,
          "end": 363.51,
          "en": "still works as before, but now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 363.51,
          "end": 367.35,
          "en": "we also got this error response handling here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 367.35,
          "end": 369.84,
          "en": "And this error response handling can also be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 369.84,
          "end": 371.73,
          "en": "in the root Route again to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 371.73,
          "end": 375.54,
          "en": "some generic skeleton for all error responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 375.54,
          "end": 377.7,
          "en": "that are not handled anywhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.7,
          "end": 380.34,
          "en": "and most importantly also for the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 380.34,
          "end": 383.67,
          "en": "that users entered an invalid URL here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 383.67,
          "end": 385.8,
          "en": "Because in that case, if I for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 385.8,
          "end": 388.803,
          "en": "try to visit local host 3000 slash ABC,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 389.67,
          "end": 393.81,
          "en": "Remix will automatically generate an error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 393.81,
          "end": 397.26,
          "en": "However, we then also have to handle that error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 397.26,
          "end": 399.84000000000003,
          "en": "And for that we can also use use catch here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 399.84000000000003,
          "end": 403.23,
          "en": "in this catch boundary in the root jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 403.23,
          "end": 407.553,
          "en": "and of course import use catch from Remix run React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 410.76,
          "end": 414.21,
          "en": "then get hold of that caught response",
          "zh": ""
        },
